-- title:
--   Order at a node place equals length on the crossing model
-- statement:
--   Let $L$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic zero, $A \subseteq L$ a valuation subring, and $F$ a field extension of $L$ that is a curve over $L$ (principal divisors exist, all place residue fields are finite over $L$, and $\Omega_{F/L}$ is free of rank one) and essentially of finite type over $L$. Let $S$ be a set of places of $F/L$, each rational (the map from $L$ to its residue field is surjective), and let $\mathcal N_0 \subseteq F$ be a local Noetherian subring. Assume: a place $P$ lies in $S$ exactly when $\mathcal N_0$ is contained in its valuation subring and every non-unit $g$ of $\mathcal N_0$ has $P.\mathrm{evalAt}\,g$ in $A$ and in the maximal ideal of $A$; every $f \in F$ satisfies $f b = \sum_i c_i a_i$ for some nonzero $b \in \mathcal N_0$, $a_i \in \mathcal N_0$ and $c_i \in L$. Let $C \subseteq L$ be a subring contained in $A$ whose image in $F$ lies in $\mathcal N_0$, with $C$ a domain and a discrete valuation ring, and $\varpi \in C$ nonzero such that for $d \in C$ the residue of $d$ in the residue field of $A$ vanishes iff $\varpi \mid d$ in $C$; assume every element of $A$ is algebraic over $C$; assume $C$-linear independence of $c : \mathrm{Fin}\,n \to L$ forces $a_i = 0$ whenever $\sum_i c_i a_i = 0$ with $a_i \in \mathcal N_0$; assume for $a, b \in A$ with $a$ in the maximal ideal and $b \neq 0$ that $b \mid a^n$ for some $n$; and assume every $g \in \mathcal N_0$ admits $o \in C$ with $g$ minus the image of $o$ a non-unit. Let $W$ be a complete discrete valuation domain, $\pi$ irreducible in $W$, $E \geq 1$, and let $\sigma : W \to \widehat{\mathcal N_0}$ (completion at the maximal ideal) send $\pi$ to the image of $\varpi$, and $\iota : \widehat{\mathcal N_0} \cong \mathrm{UVCrossingModel}\,W\,(\pi^E) = W[[X_0,X_1]]/(X_0X_1 - \pi^E)$ a ring isomorphism carrying each $\sigma o$ to the class of the constant $o$. Finally let $\mathfrak p \subset \mathcal N_0$ be a nonzero prime not containing the image of $\varpi$, let $P \in S$ satisfy $P.\mathrm{evalAt}\,g = 0 \iff g \in \mathfrak p$, let $Q$ be a prime of the crossing model contracting to $\mathfrak p$ along $\mathcal N_0 \to \widehat{\mathcal N_0} \xrightarrow{\iota} \mathrm{UVCrossingModel}\,W\,(\pi^E)$, and let $f \in \mathcal N_0$ be nonzero. Then the truncation to $\mathbb N$ of $P.\mathrm{ord}\,f$, viewed in $\mathbb N_\infty$, equals the length, over the local ring of the crossing model at $Q$, of the localisation at $Q$ of the crossing model modulo the ideal generated by $\iota$ of the image of $f$.
--
--   This is the local comparison in the place–model dictionary at a node: for a horizontal prime $\mathfrak p$ of the node ring $\mathcal N_0$, the order of vanishing of $f$ at the corresponding place of the curve agrees with the length measured on the formal crossing model $W[[X_0,X_1]]/(X_0X_1-\pi^E)$ at a prime over $\mathfrak p$, both quantities computing $v_{\mathfrak p}(f)$. It feeds the global degree identity [`AlgebraicCurve.NodeAnnulusEngine.finite_and_finsum_ord_eq_finsum_finrank_mul_length_of_ringEquiv_uvCrossingModel`](thm.html#AlgebraicCurve.NodeAnnulusEngine.finite_and_finsum_ord_eq_finsum_finrank_mul_length_of_ringEquiv_uvCrossingModel).
